From af7d78c957017f8b3a0986769f6f18e57f9362ea Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Marco Felsch <m.felsch@pengutronix.de>
Date: Tue, 26 Jul 2022 15:05:22 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ARM: dts: imx6qdl-kontron-samx6i: fix spi-flash compatible

Drop the "winbond,w25q16dw" compatible since it causes to set the
MODALIAS to w25q16dw which is not specified within spi-nor id table.
Fix this by use the common "jedec,spi-nor" compatible.

Fixes: 2125212785c9 ("ARM: dts: imx6qdl-kontron-samx6i: add Kontron SMARC SoM Support")
Signed-off-by: Marco Felsch <m.felsch@pengutronix.de>
Signed-off-by: Shawn Guo <shawnguo@kernel.org>

diff --git a/arch/arm/boot/dts/imx6qdl-kontron-samx6i.dtsi b/arch/arm/boot/dts/imx6qdl-kontron-samx6i.dtsi
index f159c58b9edb..6b791d515e29 100644
--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/imx6qdl-kontron-samx6i.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/imx6qdl-kontron-samx6i.dtsi
@@ -249,7 +249,7 @@ &ecspi4 {

 	/* default boot source: workaround #1 for errata ERR006282 */
 	smarc_flash: flash@0 {
-		compatible = "winbond,w25q16dw", "jedec,spi-nor";
+		compatible = "jedec,spi-nor";
 		reg = <0>;
 		spi-max-frequency = <20000000>;
 	};
-- 
2.25.1

You are a programming expert.

You will be given the root cause of a bug.

Based on these details, your task is to determine whether the provided code snippet contains the bug.
Think step by step.
Be conservative in your assessment. If you are unsure, answer "no."

Root cause:
The bug was caused by the use of the incompatible compatible string `"winbond,w25q16dw"` for the SPI flash device, which led to an incorrect `MODALIAS` being set. This `MODALIAS` was not recognized in the SPI-NOR ID table, resulting in potential device recognition issues and failures in proper operation.



Now, determine whether the provided code snippet is buggy:
	smarc_flash: spi-flash@0 {
		compatible = "winbond,w25q16dw", "jedec,spi-nor";
		reg = <0>;
		spi-max-frequency = <20000000>;
	};
};


